{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":154804,"duration_api_ms":150419,"num_turns":25,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dbbbbee0-79f8-4a56-ba2d-5a9c7c7e238c","total_cost_usd":0.8829839999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":62944,"cache_read_input_tokens":672928,"output_tokens":6122,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":62944,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":6122,"cacheReadInputTokens":672928,"cacheCreationInputTokens":62944,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8829839999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"Restore a directional assertion in `run_probe_chemistry_stress_with_suffix` that verifies actual molt failures or failed-molt accumulation occur under low-GH + high-NO₂ conditions. The diff removes the check (`if molt_failures == 0 && final_state.animal.failed_molt_accum <= 0.0 { record_failure(...) }`) but the scenario's doc comment still promises \"molt failures, increased mortality, condition decline\". Without this assertion, the probe only validates elevated `molt_stress_index > 0.2`, mortality, and condition decline — but not that molts actually fail. If the current model doesn't reliably produce these events, either (a) soften the assertion to check `molt_stress > threshold OR failed_molt_accum > 0` as a weaker directional claim, or (b) update the doc comment to drop the \"molt failures\" claim.","rationale":"The scenario's husbandry story (doc comment at line 616-625) explicitly says low GH + high NO₂ should cause \"molt failures\" — but the test no longer verifies this. This is a real coverage gap between what the probe documents and what it checks. The remaining `molt_stress > 0.2` assertion measures stress pressure, not actual failure events. If the model is later retuned so molt failures stop occurring under these conditions, the probe would silently pass while the narrative claims otherwise."},{"body":"Consider gating the `projected_carbonate_equilibrium()` call inside `emit_tick_snapshot` (engine.rs:122-124) behind a higher verbosity level or computing it less frequently (e.g. only on daily ticks). This solver runs on every tick when tracing is enabled, including the breeding scenario's ~1500 ticks. If the carbonate equilibrium solve is nontrivial, this could materially slow down instrumented probe runs.","rationale":"The tick snapshot emits ~20 trace notes per tick. The carbonate equilibrium computation is unique among them in that it requires solving a chemical equilibrium (not a simple field lookup). In production-length probes (1500+ hours), this scales linearly. This is not a correctness bug but a robustness/maintainability concern — if probes become slow, this would be a non-obvious hot spot. A minor concern; the reviewer considers it optional."}],"summary":"The diff is well-structured and all 6 committed tests compile and pass. The five shrimp scenario probes cover the required husbandry stories with directional/envelope assertions, the breeding probe runs ~1500 hours (exceeding the 1000+ hour requirement), and the summary test catches panics for robust reporting. The tick snapshot tracing in `emit_tick_snapshot` provides the per-tick state dumps required by the acceptance criteria. The alkalinity constant precision fix (0.1428 → 2/14.007) is correct with cross-crate synchronization tests. One substantive issue: the chemistry-stress probe's doc comment promises \"molt failures\" but the assertion validating them was removed — this is a coverage gap between narrative and test. One minor performance note about per-tick carbonate equilibrium computation in the tick snapshot."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"58182799-1c91-4aaa-a856-6ade146a571f"}
